

This is nasty.  ANSI C changed the way variable length arguments worked.
One of the reasons we really want to do ANSI C is that not only does it
let us take advantage of prototypes, but it is STANDARD.  The varargs
interface is not guaranteed to work the same way on all machines.  So,
we jump through some hoops to get ANSI if we can.

 -- Dana Jacobsen, ERL-C.
